  "retained_diagnostics": "The first unit fixture supplied a short CS limit while retaining page granularity and was rejected as an invalid loaded cache. Clearing the fixture granularity bit fixed the intended target-fault test. The original failure log is retained; production state admission was unchanged.",
  "source_reference": {
    "title": "Intel SDM Volume 2, revision 093: CMOVcc, SETcc, LOOP/LOOPcc and Jcc",
    "url": "https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/intel-sdm.html",
    "local_text": "/mnt/data/neverd-paged-scheduling-20261101/intel-sdm-vol2-093.txt"
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "SETcc and CMOVcc reuse the existing Jcc condition owner. CMOV reads before deciding; SETcc stores without reading. The native matrix checks exact operand faults, partial writes and original handler/IRET/retry.",
    "The explicit scalar binding is required and assumes CMOV availability on the bound CPU. LOOP/LOOPcc use address-sized counters, operand-sized targets and unchanged flags; target faults restart the original count. JCXZ/JECXZ never decrement. No new undefined-flags profile or memory-ordering policy is introduced.",
    "LA57 is unavailable on the recorded CPU. The remaining unlisted legacy scalars, general i386 exporter, real/VM86, tasks/call gates, debug producers, software SMM/enclave/AEX/EPCM and complete CET/FRED/event domains are not certified.",
    "This software-executor change needs no new LLVM/NeverC builtin. Global completion and the final SDK release/pin gates remain open."
  ],
